Licences of the occupation data
================================

This repository redistributes official open data and files derived from them.
Each dataset stays under its own licence. The MIT licence (LICENSE) and the
CC BY 4.0 licence (LICENSE-DOCS) do not replace those terms.

The derived database (the catalogue served by the site, plus the enrichment
and grid files) mixes several sources. Because it includes an adaptation of
Onisep data published under the Open Database License, the derived database
as a whole is shared under ODbL 1.0 (share-alike). Portions that come from
France Travail also remain under the Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0,
which requires attribution (source and date of last update).

1. Onisep — Idéo-Fiches métiers and Idéo-Métiers
------------------------------------------------
Licence: Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Sources (verified 12 November 2026):
- Idéo-Fiches métiers:
  https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/ideo-fiches-metiers
  also listed as “Licence ODBL” on https://opendata.onisep.fr/
- Idéo-Métiers Onisep:
  https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/ideo-metiers-onisep
  licence stated on data.gouv.fr: Open Data Commons Open Database License (ODbL)

Extraction included in this repository: 21 October 2026, 1,138 occupations.

You may share, create and adapt this derived database as long as you:

- attribute Onisep and keep this notice;
- share any adapted database under the same ODbL licence;
- keep the database open if you use it to produce a public work (share-alike).

Files mainly covered by this ODbL dataset:

- data/source/fiches-metiers.zip (original XML extract)
- data/source/ideo-metiers.csv
- data/source/enrichi.json (six estimated criteria per occupation)
- data/source/id-aliases.json
- public/data/catalog.json (file served by the website)
- src/generated/dataset.ts (counts and Onisep attribution generated with the catalogue)
- the Onisep-derived fields inside data/source/grille.json

The estimates (place of work, remote work, working hours, usefulness to
others, resilience to crises and automation, geographic constraint, and the
grid criteria deduced from Onisep texts) are part of the derived database.
A value whose confidence is not “high” is an estimate and must stay labelled
as such.

