How to attribute in a reuse
---------------------------
A short credit like the one already used in the website footer is enough,
for example:

    Occupation data: Onisep, Idéo-Fiches métiers (October 2026 extract),
    ODbL 1.0 — https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/ideo-fiches-metiers

    Labour-market data: France Travail, ROME 4.0 (October 2026) and
    Besoins en Main-d'Œuvre 2026, Licence Ouverte — plus the Dares
    FAP-2021 / ROME correspondence table.

    Method and grid: Tristan Vilpont, « Quel métier me correspond ? »,
    CC BY 4.0 — https://quelmetiermecorrespond.fr

If you adapt the database (new country, new sources, corrected estimates),
share your adapted database under ODbL 1.0 as well, and keep attributing
Onisep. Replace the French sources with your country's official sources
and follow those sources' own licences.
